CRITERION 2 — CB6-1 band test non-vacuity (both edges, both directions)
  Target: internal/services/insights/trends.go:99-107 (MajorExpenseTrends'
  classifier; the second +-5 site at :171-173 belongs to CategoryTrends and
  was correctly left alone).
  a) Unmutated: `go test -count=1 ./internal/services/insights/ -run
     TestAnalyzeMajorExpenseTrends_DirectionBandEdges -v` -> PASS, all 4
     subtests PASS.
  b) Mutant ±5 -> ±0 (`case changePercent > 0:` / `< -0:`), same command:
     FAIL, exit 1.
       "exactly +5 is stable, not up": Direction = "up"
        (changePercent=5.0000000000), want "stable"  -- FAIL
       "exactly -5 is stable, not down": Direction = "down"
        (changePercent=-5.0000000000), want "stable" -- FAIL
     => the test kills the ±0 mutation the spec named.
  c) Mutant ±5 -> ±10 (`> 10:` / `< -10:`), same command: FAIL, exit 1.
       "just past +5 is up": Direction = "stable"
        (changePercent=5.0100000000), want "up"      -- FAIL
       "just past -5 is down": Direction = "stable"
        (changePercent=-5.0100000000), want "down"   -- FAIL
     => the OUTER side of the band is pinned too; band pinned in both
     directions, not just one.
  d) Fixtures land EXACTLY on the edge (not merely inside it). Proof by a
     third mutant `case changePercent >= 5:` / `<= -5:`: the two "exactly"
     subtests FLIP to up/down and FAIL. Combined with (a) passing under the
     strict `> 5` / `< -5`, that brackets changePercent to be neither >5
     nor <5 -- i.e. bit-exactly +5.0 (and -5.0). Fixtures read from the
     test source: prev=100 / cur=105 -> +5 stable; cur=105.01 -> up;
     cur=95 -> -5 stable; cur=94.99 -> down, with the Jan-15 txn landing in
     the derived previous window (prevStart Jan 4 .. prevEnd Jan 31).
  e) No production-code change: `git diff 0a697b1 --stat` lists
     trends_test.go only; trends.go is not in the diff.
  RESULT: MET.

