OBSERVATIONS (not failures; for the lead's backlog / checker-a11y)
  O1. The drill buttons' accessible name is the row's FULL visible text
      ("Pharmacy$40.00  1.1%", "Unmatched-$12.34"), not the group name
      alone. CB6-3 says "accessible name = the group name (visible text
      suffices)", and the whole row is visible text, so this is within the
      letter of the spec -- but it is checker-a11y's call whether the
      concatenated amount is acceptable as the name.
  O2. TestRenderKPIMonthDetail_ExpensesPositiveTotalIsRed and
      TestRenderKPIMonthDetail_SavingsPositiveTotalIsGreen also pass
      against the un-fixed master template (proven in vt/muttpl); they are
      characterization tests. The behavior change is guarded solely by
      ExpensesNegativeTotalIsGreen, which does kill the mutation.
  O3. CB6-5 ships no regression test (the spec's permitted option). The
      order-pinning is therefore guarded by a comment and by code position
      only: a future edit moving the sort back above the loop would be
      caught by no test.
  O4. Pre-existing, unrelated to CB6: .swarm/flags/ND3.flag and
